<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Sentinum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/295-bce">295 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-samnite-war">Third Samnite War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Sentinum was fought in 295 BCE near Sentinum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umbria">Umbria</a>, close to modern Sassoferrato, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and a coalition of Samnites and Senone <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gauls">Gauls</a>, with Etruscan and Umbrian backing. The consuls <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintus-fabius-maximus">Quintus Fabius Maximus</a> Rullianus and Publius Decius Mus won a hard-fought victory, in which Decius was said to have sacrificed himself. It was the decisive battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-samnite-war">Third Samnite War</a> and opened central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> to Roman domination.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Rome defeated the Latins in 340–338 BCE, the Samnites in three wars ending in 290 BCE, and their allies at the <b>Battle of Sentinum</b> in 295 BCE.</blockquote><a href="/empire/roman-republic">Roman Republic · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The city came under Roman control after the wars of the early 3rd century, traditionally around the <b>battle of Sentinum</b> in 295 BCE, and remained a modest Roman town; Etruscan burials continued there into the 1st century BCE.</blockquote><a href="/state/clusium">Clusium</a></li><li><blockquote>The Samnites trapped a Roman army at the Caudine Forks in 321 BCE but lost at <b>Sentinum</b> in 295 BCE and accepted Roman alliance in 290 BCE.</blockquote><a href="/state/samnite-league">Samnite League</a></li><li><blockquote>The Senones fought alongside the Samnites at <b>Sentinum</b> in 295 BCE.</blockquote><a href="/state/senones-400">Senones</a></li><li><blockquote>Rome founded Narnia in 299 BCE, and after the <b>battle of Sentinum</b> in 295 BCE, where some Umbrians backed the anti-Roman coalition, the Umbrian towns became allies.</blockquote><a href="/state/umbrians">Umbrians</a></li></ul></section>
